      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Quick Start for CloudFlow CLI**\n\nBefore you can start using CloudFlow CLI, ensure you have the necessary prerequisites in place.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n* **Python**: CloudFlow CLI requires Python 3.9 or later. Install the latest version of Python on your machine if you haven't already.\n* **Docker**: CloudFlow CLI uses Docker for deployment. Ensure Docker is installed and running on your machine.\n* **AWS IAM Access Key**: You'll need an AWS IAM Access Key to authenticate with CloudFlow CLI. Store this key securely and use it when prompted.\n\n**Getting Started**\n\nTo start using CloudFlow CLI, follow these steps:\n\n1. Install CloudFlow CLI using `pip install cloudflow-cli`. This will install the necessary libraries and tools required for the command-line interface.\n2. Run `cloudflow auth login --key [YOUR_KEY]` in your terminal, replacing `[YOUR_KEY]` with your AWS IAM Access Key. This will authenticate your account and set up the necessary access to CloudFlow.\n3. Mark the environment as `prod` and deploy your application using `cloudflow deploy --env prod`. This will kick off the deployment process and configure your target environment.",
